# Generated artifacts must arrive in the working tree exactly as their
# generator wrote them.
#
# `lib/contracts.test.ts` compares data/cities-report.md byte-for-byte against
# what `scripts/ingest-cities.mjs` would emit, which is the only thing making
# the GeoNames CC BY 4.0 attribution contract enforceable rather than
# decorative. The generators write LF. Git stores LF. But `core.autocrlf=true`
# — the Windows default, and set on this repo — rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout, so a FRESH CLONE ON WINDOWS failed that contract on line endings
# alone, for a reason with nothing to do with attribution. CI never saw it
# because CI is Linux.
#
# A licence guard that goes red for a spurious reason is a guard people learn
# to ignore, so pin the eol rather than relaxing the comparison.
data/*.md   text eol=lf
data/*.json text eol=lf

# The same rule, one directory further out, for the same reason.
#
# `scripts/build-provinces.mjs` writes each province file as one line of JSON
# plus a trailing LF, and measures the bytes it is about to write against the
# gzip budget. `lib/provinceTopology.test.ts` re-measures the file ON DISK
# against that same budget. Nothing under `public/` was pinned before this, so
# a fresh Windows clone would take a CRLF copy of all 247 files and measure
# bytes the generator never wrote — the artifact would no longer be what its
# own build produced, which is the property the gate exists to hold.
#
# `public/climate/*.json` is pinned in the same breath: Plan 5 creates that
# directory, and until it does the line is inert.
public/provinces/*.json text eol=lf
public/climate/*.json   text eol=lf

# And the projection manifest, which is one line of JSON plus a trailing LF.
# `data/projections-report.md` publishes its exact byte and gzip sizes, and
# `scripts/build-projections.mjs` measures them on the bytes it writes. Left
# unpinned, a fresh Windows clone takes a CRLF copy that is one byte longer
# than the report says it is, and the record stops describing the artifact.
public/country-projections.json text eol=lf
